# Schneider Electric iEM3155.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | Schneider Electric iEM3155 (iEM3100/3200/3300 series) — Modbus map for Omni Console
# | 
# | Source: Schneider "iEM3100/iEM3200/iEM3300 series" user manual (DOCA0005EN)
# | Modbus register list, cross-checked against a working field configuration.
# | - Instantaneous values are FLOAT32 (f32), 2 registers, Big-Endian — the
# | default — so `word_order` is omitted. Energy totals are 64-bit integers
# | (s64, 4 registers, Big-Endian) in Wh. Read with FC03 (holding).
# | - IMPORTANT addressing: the manual prints 1-based "register" numbers; the
# | on-the-wire (PDU) address is register - 1. Addresses below are the 0-based
# | PDU addresses that match how Omni Console issues reads (e.g. manual reg 3060
# | "Total active power" -> address 3059). Power is reported in kW / kvar / kVA.
# | - Factory defaults: device address (slave) = 1, RTU = 19.2 kbps, 8E1.
# | - Additional energy registers (reactive/apparent, per-direction) exist in
# | DOCA0005EN around manual reg 3220+ and can be appended as needed.
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Schneider Electric
@model=iEM3155
@vendor_website=se.com
@description=Energy meter — current, voltage L-L/L-N, total power, power factor, frequency (float) and 64-bit active energy import/export totals.
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/schneider-iem3155.toml; Source: Schneider "iEM3100/iEM3200/iEM3300 series" user manual (DOCA0005EN). Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
@x_status=unverified
@x_origin=omniconsole

